hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19207","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Ikrimah meaning Ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Tariq ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qurashi narrated to me, he said: Rafi ibn Rifaah came to the gathering of the Ansar and said: Our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us today something that used to help us in our livelihood. He forbade us renting out land. He said: Whoever has land let him cultivate it, or let him give it to his brother to cultivate, or let him leave it. He forbade us the earnings of the cupper, and ordered us to feed it to our water-carrying camels. He forbade us the earnings of the slave girl except what she earns with her hand, and he said like this with his fingers, like bread, spinning, and carding wool."
